// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`root help groups > fits 100 columns and reads the same every time 1`] = `
"Usage: cao [options] [command]

Code Agent Orchestrator: run YAML-defined workflows as isolated coding-agent sessions

Options:
  -V, --version                  output the version number
  -h, --help                     display help for command

Run:
  run [options] [workflow]       Run a workflow
  resume [options] [run]         Resume an interrupted, failed or paused run
  ui [options] [run]             Open the workspace on a run, or pick one
  stop [options] [run]           Stop a run from another terminal
  validate [options] [workflow]  Validate a workflow and print its execution plan

Inspect:
  status [options] [run]         Show a run and its tasks
  list [options]                 List the runs of this repository
  logs [options] [refs...]       Show or follow a task transcript
  peek [options] [refs...]       Peek into a running worker
  diff [options] [refs...]       Show what a task changed
  report [options] [run]         Render a run as a document to paste into a pull request

Task controls:
  task                           Show one task, or steer it: show (default) | stop | restart | edit

Diagnostics:
  doctor [options] [config]      Check this machine: Node, git, the agent CLIs, and what past runs
                                 left behind
  clean [options] [run]          Remove the worktrees and branches a run created
  emit [options] [action]        Turn announcing runs to the desktop app on or off, and show what it
                                 is doing

Commands:
  help [command]                 display help for command

Exit codes:
  0    completed                     1    failed
  2    usage or validation error     3    paused (approval or input required)
  70   internal error                130  interrupted (Ctrl+C or cao stop)

Environment:
  CAO_CLAUDE_COMMAND   Claude CLI to launch instead of \`claude\`
  CAO_CODEX_COMMAND    Codex CLI to launch instead of \`codex\`
  CAO_EMIT             announce runs to a desktop app on this machine (1/0); see cao emit status
  CAO_HOME             override ~/.cao, the directory cao announces runs into (docs/desktop.md)
  CAO_DEBUG            print stack traces when a command fails
  CAO_ASCII            draw tables and status marks in ASCII (CAO_UNICODE=1 forces glyphs back on)
  CAO_ALT_SCREEN       0 draws the workspace in the normal buffer (also --no-alt-screen)
  CAO_THEME            workspace theme: default|mono (also --theme)
  CAO_REDUCED_MOTION   1 stops the spinner and the activity pulse
  NO_COLOR/FORCE_COLOR disable or force ANSI colour (also --color)
  COLUMNS              width to lay tables out in when there is no terminal to ask

"
`;
